silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_3__step_joc_§15_1_factorization_systems a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Joy of Cats section 15.1 says: in a factorization system, every morphism factors uniquely as a right factor (the gate/epi) followed by a left factor (the admit/mono). The type step is one such factorization: gate is the epi part (checking sort), admit is the mono part (embedding into the typed leg)." .
